# Keep documentation current

After **any** feature, fix, rename, platform change, or new behavior, update **all** user-facing and developer docs in the same turn. Do not leave docs for “later”.

## Files that must stay in sync

| File | Language | Role |
|------|----------|------|
| `docs/README.md` | EN | Full product README (canonical) |
| `docs/README.ru.md` | RU | Same content as EN product README |
| `README.md` (repo root) | EN short | Pointer to `docs/`; keep **Owner / Developer = Nanda** |
| `docs/Technical/TECHNICAL.md` | EN | Full technical doc (canonical; includes iOS cheatsheet §14) |
| `docs/Technical/TECHNICAL.ru.md` | RU | Same facts as EN TECHNICAL |
| `docs/Technical/DEV_BLOG.md` | EN | Chronological Dev Blog (development diary) |
| `docs/Technical/DEV_BLOG.ru.md` | RU | Same stages as EN Dev Blog |
| `docs/Legal-En/` · `Legal-Ru/` · `Legal-Hu/` | EN / RU / HU | Privacy, Terms, Cookies — index from product README, **not** per-folder README files |
| `docs/LICENSE` | — | Canonical LGPL-3.0-only; root `LICENSE` mirrors it |

There is **no** `DEVELOPER.md`. iOS quick start lives only in Technical §14 (EN + RU).

EN and RU pairs must match on facts (bundle IDs, commands, languages, contacts, APIs). If you change one, change the other.

## Naming / identity

- **README, Technical, contacts:** owner / developer is **Nanda** (plus existing emails, Telegram, Discord, GitHub, site).
- **Legal docs only:** full legal creator name **Adnan Huseynli (Nanda)** may appear.
- Do **not** put “Adnan Huseynli” in product README or Technical identity tables.

## What to update when

- **Identity** (name, bundle IDs, contacts, GitHub, owner line): `docs/README` EN+RU + root short README + Technical EN+RU.
- **How to run / iOS / Android / signing**: `docs/README` + Technical §14–18.
- **API, login, 2FA, cache, languages, themes, removed features**: Technical EN+RU (honesty table if completeness changed).
- **Major development stages / decisions**: append matching entries to `docs/Technical/DEV_BLOG.md` + `DEV_BLOG.ru.md`.
- **User-visible features**: `docs/README` feature list EN+RU.
- **Version bumps** (`1.x.y` marketing): follow `.cursor/rules/versioning.mdc` — `pubspec`, platform mirrors, Settings (three numbers only), README + TECHNICAL + DEV_BLOG EN+RU.
- **Privacy / terms / cookies behavior**: matching files under `docs/Legal-*` (all three languages when facts change).

## Honesty

Document what the code actually does. If something is untested (e.g. live ELTE login), say so.

## End of task

Before finishing a change, scan the files above for stale paths, IDs, commands, or claims. Cross-link EN ↔ RU and README ↔ Technical ↔ Legal indexes. Do not recreate `docs/Legal-*/README.md` or `DEVELOPER.md`.
